    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## SETUP TODOs\n1. Replace `documentId` on every Google Sheets node below with your Household Ledger spreadsheet ID (see household-ledger-sheets-schema.md)\n2. Connect your Google Sheets credential (reused the same credential ID as your BNS workflows below \u2014 adjust if this is a different Google account)\n3. Activate this workflow, then grab the Production webhook URL from the Webhook node \u2014 that's what the mobile app POSTs to\n4. Create the `LastSavedList` tab (see household-ledger-sheets-schema.md) \u2014 same columns as `ShoppingList`. Needed for the `finalize`/`recall` pair below.\n\nExpected POST body:\n`{ \"action\": \"get\" }`\n`{ \"action\": \"upsert\", \"item\": \"Basmati Rice\", \"category\": \"Pantry\", \"store\": \"Walmart\", \"price\": 9.52, \"qty\": 1, \"cadence\": \"Week\" }`\n`{ \"action\": \"remove\", \"item\": \"Basmati Rice\" }`\n`{ \"action\": \"clear\" }` \u2014 empties every ShoppingList row (keeps the header)\n`{ \"action\": \"finalize\" }` \u2014 doesn't change ShoppingList; sends a Telegram summary of the current list + total, and snapshots the list into LastSavedList (clear+append) so it survives a later `clear`. Same response shape as `get`.\n`{ \"action\": \"recall\" }` \u2014 added 2026-08-09, upserts every row from LastSavedList into ShoppingList (merges on top, matched on item \u2014 same as a normal upsert), letting next week's list start from last week's finalized one. Same response shape as `get`.\n\nResponse: `{ \"list\": [...rows], \"total\": 42.10, \"budget\": 200, \"remaining\": 157.90 }`\n\nConfirmed live 2026-08-08: Clear All and Save List (finalize+Telegram) both working end-to-end, Send Finalize Summary's real bot credential wired with On Error set to Continue.\n\nSETUP TODO for `recall`/snapshot (2026-08-09, not yet applied live): the new LastSavedList-clearing chain (`Get LastSavedList Rows to Clear` \u2192 ... \u2192 `Snapshot to LastSavedList`) has `onError: continueRegularOutput` pre-set in this file rather than left to configure live, since we now know that field name \u2014 worth a quick visual double-check in the node Settings tab once live, same as was done for Send Finalize Summary. Also double check the `rowsToDelete` field name on `Clear LastSavedList Rows` the same way it was verified on `Clear ShoppingList Rows`.",
        "height": 460,
        "width": 380
      },
